{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>That his heart not be lifted up above his brothers</b> — the parashah begins and ends with the language of רמות (exaltation), a hint that kingship departed from Judah, whose name ascends to ל״ה (35), corresponding to ל״ה degrees of kingship; and David was בן ל״ה (35 years old) when he reigned, and therefore he composed a song that begins with ל״ה — namely, למנצח לעבד ה׳ לדוד (For the Leader, a Psalm of David the servant of YHWH):"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:09:58.451357614Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}